Maybe out of the scope of this post but still related to the BumpMapNode subject.
It would be really useful to have the choice of the channel to use. It is currently hardcoded to `x` but often rgba channels can be used for multiple purposes.

```js
class BumpMapNode extends TempNode {
  constructor(node, uvNode = uv(), channel = 'x', scaleNode = 1) {
    super('vec3');

    this.node = node;
    this.uvNode = uvNode;
    this.channel = channel;
    this.scaleNode = scaleNode;
  }
}
```

The prop would then be fed into `dHdxy_fwd`

or maybe accept something other than a texture. e.g. split(bumpNode, 'r'), however I am unsure how to do as `dHdxy_fwd` uses dFdx/dFdy
